# The Logi Bolt receiver asserts USB remote wakeup as soon as the machine
# suspends, so it resumes a few seconds later and suspend never sticks - with
# the receiver unplugged the same laptop stays asleep. Nothing tells the
# difference between that and a real key press, so the receiver is simply not
# allowed to wake the machine any more; its mouse and keyboard still work, and
# the laptop's own keyboard and the power button still wake it.
#
# Only this receiver: the wired keyboard on another port keeps its wakeup, and
# so would any other device. For a second Logitech dongle (Unifying receivers
# are 046d:c52b and friends), add its id here - `lsusb` prints it.
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="046d", ATTR{idProduct}=="c548", ATTR{power/wakeup}="disabled"
